涂炭，尽做些家破人亡，祸害百姓之事。摄政王何曾意识到，他如此荒淫的行径，越发激起民怨，广结仇恨，这世间，想他死之人何其之多。凤傲天心知肚明，这一时的风平浪静，不过是转瞬即逝，如今她未死成，那些想她死之人怕是夜不能寐，许是在某处密会私谋，如何置她与死地。脑海中掠过这具身体临死前的种种，想着她虽荒淫无度，却也不傻，知晓杀她之人数不胜数，又怎会只身离开军营，前往那人迹罕至之地？她一向将心思隐藏地极好，何人会知晓她悖逆人伦，爱上自己的皇兄，两年前驾崩的先皇？引她前去之人与先皇有着一样的容貌身形，而先皇便是她的死穴，但凡有一丝理智，她亦是不顾一切地追赶着那恍若隔世的身影而去。可见此人谋划已久，深知她的心思，对她了若指掌，否则，怎会将她身旁武功最高的魂魄二人引开，虽然隐卫拼死护主，终究还是逃不过被杀的命运。回首往昔，不过是过眼云烟，她与她，亦是往事如烟罢了，因她直至死那一刻，亦是嘴角含笑。令她不解的是，依着她的武功，不会如此轻而易举被旁人得逞，这其中必定是有所遗漏？凤傲天静立与营帐外的草地上，左手背与身后，右手握着一块羊脂白玉，纤细的玉指似有若无地抚摸着暖玉，月影笼罩，指尖渗着薄薄的凉意。青衣踌躇徐步向前，一双清眸打量着那肃立与营帐之外的摄政王，冷峻如霜的侧脸，身着锦缎中衣，不寒而栗，冷冽如风。冷风袭来，他顿觉寒意丛生，连忙收敛起窥探的双眸，稍作整理，眉目含春，勾唇浅笑，清秀俊俏的容貌，衬着这清冷的月色，反倒多了几分妩媚，迈着轻柔的步子加快了脚步。这几日，他算得上是摄政王最宠爱之人，想着他堂堂七尺男儿，却要学那女子娇态，委身承欢与一名男子，每每想起，便觉恶寒。但，事已至此，又怎可半途而废，他苟且偷生，甘当世人不齿的娈人，只因这摄政王不喜杜若，便下令凡是谁家栽种杜若者，灭其九族，满门抄斩。可怜他全家十余口人，只因他的厌恶，落得个灭门之祸，莫不是他侥幸逃脱，如今，怕也落得个身首异处。隐去心中的恨意，脚步轻快地上前，身体也不自觉地向凤傲天贴去，娇声唤道，“王爷，您真坏，适才……”双手还未碰上凤傲天的手臂，顺口娇嗔的话还未说完，便对上一双冷若寒潭的双眸，这样的摄政王，让他心生胆寒。他身形一顿，还未将剩下的话说出口，身体却被一阵冷风卷起，待他反应过来时，“噗通”一声，人已跌入一里之外的冰湖之中。凤傲天嫌恶地看了一眼适才挥他出去不小心沾染上他身上散发出的浓厚呛人的香粉气息的袖摆，抬起背在身后的左手，食指对准那袖摆划过，一片锦缎便随风而去。湖水凛冽刺骨，青衣与湖中挣扎半天，才爬上岸，全身虚脱，躺在冰冷的地上喘气，自摄政王回来，原以为他会大发雷霆，亦或是传召男宠出气，未曾料到，他却一言不发回了营帐，仿佛适才凶险之事与他无关。他暗自思忖，今日两番被他冷视，难道摄政王已厌烦与他？还是对他有所怀疑？想到这处，他猛地自地上坐起，心神难安，转念一想，并非如此，若是当真怀疑与他，如今，他已经成为一具死尸。怀着惴惴不安的心思，青衣拖着湿漉漉的青衫，狼狈不堪地向军营走去，不行，他不能就这样放弃，事到如今，由不得他，即便是死，也要拼死一试。凤傲天并未步入帐内，而是冷然伫立，她断定，此人接近她，必定心怀不轨，不过，她更想知晓的是，他背后指使之人到底是谁？青衣瑟缩地返回军营，刺骨冷风，无情地划过他本已浑身湿透的单薄身子，他嘴角冻得青紫，倔强地咬紧牙关。适才的突发事件，不少士兵看在眼里，他们深知摄政王的脾气，如此的惩罚已经算是轻的，但，看着青衣如此狼狈，还是不免投来了些许的同情。青衣尽量挺直腰背，这等屈辱算得了什么，比起床笫之间，那非人的疼痛折磨，他还要装出一副极其享受的姿态，这实在算不得什么。身体已近麻木，抬眸，却见摄政王并未回营帐，依旧是如冰峰般矗立，他扯动着冻僵的嘴角，低垂着眼脸，颤颤巍巍地行至凤傲天面前，跪下，凄然道，“奴惹王爷不悦，请王爷责罚。”－－－－－－题外话－－－－－－嘿嘿……亲耐哒们，喜欢的话记得收藏哦！嗷呜……谢谢亲耐哒邪邪、微微、幽幽、鹅鹅、灵、墨墨送的花花，么么哒！谢谢亲耐哒宝宝送的评价票票和打赏，么么哒！谢谢亲耐哒鹅鹅送的评价票，么么哒！", "source": "www.quanwenyuedu.io", "source_url": "https://www.quanwenyuedu.io/n/yetaicanbao/2.html", "_fixed": true, "content_en": "Volume 1 Regency Storm 002 Please punish me. The moon is like frost. At dusk on the top of the black mountain, the cold light shines on the iron clothes. Feng Aotian was not sleepy at all. When she was sleeping with the wolves, night was a good time to look for food. Later, she became a shadow. Whenever the night was cold and windy, it was the time for her to kill with bloodlust. Now, she didn't have to hunt for food or kill people. The arrow wound on her chest had been expertly bandaged. On the first day of her rebirth, she was rarely at leisure. The night is lonely. If it were normal, the regent's camp would be filled with music and singing every night. The music was endless and could be heard hundreds of miles away. How could such a luxurious state look like marching and fighting? Such behavior is like a prince taking his beautiful family to enjoy the mountains and rivers, which is very comfortable. But it really corresponds to the poem, \"The merchant women don't know the hatred of the country's subjugation, but they still sing the queen's love across the river.\" However, this regent was not close to women and only loved men. He raised three thousand beautiful men in the harem and abused them every night. It has been five days since we arrived at the border. All the soldiers in the army who are good-looking will be summoned into his tent by him. If they don't obey, they will be cut into pieces with a thousand swords, which is a small punishment, and they can be torn apart alive. She had an eccentric temperament, and would get angry if she was not careful. In just a few days, he had killed thousands of generals in the camp. Everyone in the army, from the general to the soldiers, swallowed their anger and complained, but dared not speak out. This was because the regent was truly loved by God. He had cultivated profound martial arts, was superb and invincible, and his methods were cruel. No one dared to compete with him. Nowadays, the morale of the army is low. How can they think of swearing allegiance to the death and guarding the border? They just hope that this evil star will die immediately. Don't let your soul be ruined again and do things that destroy your family and harm the people. The regent had never realized that his debauched behavior would arouse public resentment and engender hatred. There were so many people in the world who wanted him dead. Feng Aotian knew very well that the peace and calm at this moment was just fleeting. Now that she was not dead, those who wanted her to die were afraid that they could not sleep at night. Maybe they were secretly meeting somewhere to plot how to kill her. All the things that happened to this body before it died passed through my mind, thinking that although she was debauched, she was not stupid. She knew that there were countless people who wanted to kill her, so how could she leave the military camp alone and go to that inaccessible place? She has always hidden her thoughts very well. Who would know that she rebelled against human ethics and fell in love with her royal brother, the late emperor who died two years ago? The person who led her there had the same appearance and figure as the late emperor, and the late emperor was her Achilles heel. As long as she had a shred of sense, she would chase after the figure who seemed to be from another world at all costs. It can be seen that this person has been planning for a long time, knows her thoughts well, and knows her well. Otherwise, how could he lead the two souls with the highest martial arts skills around her away. Although the hidden guard fought to the death to protect the master, he could not escape the fate of being killed. Looking back on the past, it was just a passing cloud, and the past with her was just like smoke, because she had a smile on her lips until the moment she died. What puzzles her is that with her martial arts, others cannot succeed so easily. There must be something missing in this? Feng Aotian stood quietly on the grass outside the tent, holding a piece of mutton-fat white jade in his right hand on the back of his left hand and his right hand. His slender jade fingers seemed to be caressing the warm jade, the moon shadow shrouded her, and her fingertips were filled with a thin coolness. Qing Yi hesitated and stepped forward slowly, with a pair of clear eyes looking at the regent who stood solemnly outside the tent. His profile was as cold as frost, and he was wearing a brocade coat, shuddering, as cold as the wind. The cold wind hit him, and he suddenly felt chilly. He quickly restrained his prying eyes and straightened himself out. His brows were springy, his lips were curled up in a smile, and his delicate and handsome appearance seemed a bit more charming against the cold moonlight. He quickened his pace with gentle steps. These days, he can be regarded as the most beloved person of the regent. Thinking about his dignified seven-foot-tall man, but he wants to imitate the woman's coquettish manner and commit himself to a man, every time he thinks about it, he feels cold. However, now that the matter has come to this, how can he give up halfway? He lives an ignoble existence and is willing to be a despised prostitute. Just because the regent doesn't like Du Ruo, he orders anyone who has planted Du Ruo to have his nine clans exterminated and his entire family beheaded. It's pity that his whole family of more than ten people were wiped out just because of his disgust. Maybe he escaped by chance, but now, I'm afraid he will also end up with his body and head missing. Hiding the hatred in his heart, he stepped forward briskly, his body unconsciously leaning towards Feng Aotian, and he called out sweetly, \"My lord, you are so bad, just now...\" Before his hands touched Feng Aotian's arm, and before he finished his smooth and charming words, he met a pair of eyes as cold as a cold pool. Such a regent made him feel terrified. He paused, and before he could say the rest of his words, his body was swept up by a gust of cold wind. When he reacted, there was a \"pop\" and he had fallen into the icy lake a mile away. Feng Aotian glanced with disgust at the sleeve hem that he had just waved out and was accidentally contaminated by the strong, choking powder smell emitting from his body. He raised his left hand behind his back, aimed his index finger at the sleeve hem, and then a piece of brocade went away with the wind. The water in the lake was biting and biting. Qing Yi struggled in the lake for a long time before he climbed ashore. He was exhausted and lay on the cold ground panting. Since the regent came back, he thought he would get angry or summon his male favorite to vent his anger. Unexpectedly, he returned to the camp without saying a word, as if the dangerous incident just now had nothing to do with him. He secretly thought to himself that he had been looked down upon twice by him today. Could it be that the regent was tired of dealing with him? Or do you still have doubts about him? Thinking of this, he suddenly sat up from the ground, feeling uneasy. Then he thought, that was not the case. If he really doubted him, he would be a dead body now. With anxious thoughts, Qing Yi drags his wet shirt and walks towards the military camp in embarrassment. No, he can't give up like this. Now that things have come to an end, he can't help it. Even if he dies, he has to give it a try. Feng Aotian did not step into the tent, but stood there coldly. She concluded that this person must have evil intentions when approaching her. However,", "title_en": "Chapter 2"}